'''Inspired Learning''' is a [[unique]] {{il|Crimson Jewel}}.

==Mechanics==
[[File:Inspired Learning sockets 3.16.1.png|thumb|430px|Inspired Learning jewel sockets in Path of Exile 3.16.1. Blue circles denote the small radius around the jewel socket. Note how at least 4 notable skills are within each radius.]]
Upon [[kill]]ing a {{c|rare|rare}} [[monster]], the [[character]] gains '''''one''''' of its [[modifier]]s for the next 20 seconds. As a special exception, this item's on-kill effect works with [[minion]]s and [[proxies]]. Note that although when capturing a beast, the beast will drop loot, but it does not count as killing.

This jewel can be considered a low-power version of the similar stat on {{il|Headhunter}}, which provides the ability to gain '''all''' [[monster modifiers]] from a slain rare enemy. Because stolen modifiers cannot stack,<ref>https://old.reddit.com/r/pathofexile/comments/v317cb/3180e_patch_notes_restartless_headhunter_now/iavrgh5/?context=4</ref> there is no benefit to combining Inspired Learning with Headhunter; it will only reduce the duration of one stolen modifier from 60 seconds to 20. 

However, multiple copies of Inspired Learning can stack (e.g. regular and Foulborn version), so that up to 2 new monster modifiers can steal from slayed monster, as longer as they are not in the existing mod pool the player already have. In case of getting the existing mod the player has, the jewel will refresh the timer of that mod.

Stolen modifiers can grant [[buff]]s (e.g. [[Accuracy_and_Crits_Aura|{{c|normal|Precision Aura}}]]) but are not inherently buffs themselves; they have no green-bordered icon, and do not interact with buff-specific stats like {{il|Mantra of Flames}}. 

The following modifiers can '''''not''''' be gained by characters:
* {{ml|MonsterNemesisSpawnsMonsters}}
* {{ml|MonsterNemesisUniqueDrop}}
* {{ml|MonsterNemesisRaisesAfterDeath}}

The Inspired Learning jewel can only grant its effect when placed in one of the jewel sockets shown in the image, with 4 allocated [[notable]] passives inside its radius. It has no effect when socketed in a socket of a [[Cluster Jewel]]. 

[[Oil|Anointing]] a notable passive despite does not involve spending passive skill point, but the jewel still counted as allocated a notable within the jewel radius.
